<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-1384] Compute job ids duplication</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-1384</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Configure custom CollisionSpi with any implemenation which keeps waiting jobs list not empty. Execute considerable amount of tasks (e.g. 10000) from 2 or more nodes with jobs mapped to one node.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Error occurs on mapped node: &quot;Received computation request with duplicate job ID (could be network malfunction, source node may hang if task timeout was not set)&quot;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Reason: TaskGridWorker:processMappedJobs generates job ids as following: IgniteUuid jobId = IgniteUuid.fromUuid(node.id()); &lt;br/&gt;
where node.id() is identifier of node the job is mapped to. So parallel generation of job ids on different nodes leads to ids duplication.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Possible solution: use node.id() of local node in job id generation.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
